<p>Listen, strange men building houses in the middle of the road is no basis for a system of culture. Supreme societal cohesion derives from interpersonal communication, not some farcical mid-boulevard construction site.</p>
<p>That being said, I'm not sure I'm getting the connection between the note at the end and the rest, beyond the cities being extensive. That seems to (maybe?) be an actual civilization, with sailing capabilities and the ability to brainwash/coerce the sailors into joining them in going&#8230;somewhere?</p>

